From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shrek Shao <shrekshao@google.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:03:27 -0700
Subject: [gl] Add compute blit for Sint and Uint texture formats

This CL:
- Adds toggles UseBlitForUintTextureToBufferCopy and
  UseBlitForSintTextureToBufferCopy, enabled by default on OpenGLES.
- Implements compute shader blits for integer (Uint and Sint) textures
  in BlitTextureToBuffer.
- Routes integer formats to compute shader blits on OpenGLES except
  RGBA32Uint and RGBA32Sint, which are the only integer formats
  guaranteed by the OpenGL ES 3.1 spec to be supported by glReadPixels
  with matching data layout.
- Bypasses compute shader blit for integer cube textures in compat mode.
  In WGSL, texture_cube<u32> and texture_cube<i32> do not support
  textureSampleLevel or textureLoad, and textureGather only operates on
  mip level 0 for a single component. Therefore, integer cube textures
  fall back to glReadPixels via FramebufferTexture2D for each cube face.
- Expands CopyTests_T2B and CopyTests_T2B_Compat format parameters to
  cover integer formats.

Bug: 556959073, 562077184
Change-Id: Ica78ec08b6702ea386c7d95e36b5f2fd43a1b02b
